From: Kirill =?UTF-8?q?M=C3=BCller?= <kirill@cynkra.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Reserve the block allocator pool without accounting it

The pool is reserved whole in the constructor, as large as the memory
limit, and the kernel's heuristic overcommit counts a private writable
mapping that size when the process forks: one holding databases can
fail to start a child, as the tests do through callr.
MAP_NORESERVE leaves the reservation out of that count; the pages are
still committed as they are touched. duckdb/duckdb@55b94c4801 (the
v1.5-variegata merge) reserves the pool only once a size is set.
---
 src/duckdb/src/storage/block_allocator.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/storage/block_allocator.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/storage/block_allocator.cpp
index 233b545562..3b65bf1c7c 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/storage/block_allocator.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/storage/block_allocator.cpp
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ static data_ptr_t AllocateVirtualMemory(const idx_t size) {
 	// This returns nullptr on failure
 	return data_ptr_t(VirtualAlloc(nullptr, size, MEM_RESERVE, PAGE_NOACCESS));
 #else
-	const auto ptr = mmap(nullptr, size, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANONYMOUS, -1, 0);
+	const auto ptr = mmap(nullptr, size, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANONYMOUS | MAP_NORESERVE, -1, 0);
 	return ptr == MAP_FAILED ? nullptr : data_ptr_cast(ptr);
 #endif
 }
